# Backend Mappers

Controllers return contract DTOs — never raw Mongoose documents or lean objects without mapping.

## Pattern

- Static class extending `BaseMapper` (e.g. `UserMappers`).
- `toDto(source)` — single document or ObjectId (IdName fallback via `BaseMapper.objectIdToString`).
- `toDtos(source)` — array mapping.
- `toDtosPaged(source: PaginateResult<T>)` — `PagedListDto<T>` for list endpoints.

```ts
export class UserMappers extends BaseMapper {
  static toDtosPaged(source: PaginateResult<User>): PagedListDto<UserDto> {
    return {
      docs: UserMappers.toDtos(source.docs) as UserDto[],
      totalDocs: source.totalDocs,
      limit: source.limit,
      page: source.page,
      totalPages: source.totalPages,
    };
  }

  static toDto(source: User | Types.ObjectId): UserDto | string {
    if (!this.isValidDocument(source)) {
      return BaseMapper.objectIdToString(source);
    }
    const user = source as User;
    return { id: user._id.toHexString(), /* ... */ };
  }
}
```

## Controller usage

```ts
@Get()
list(@Query() query: GetUsersQuery) {
  return UserMappers.toDtosPaged(await this.usersService.get(query));
}

@Get(':id')
get(@Param('id') id: string) {
  return UserMappers.toDto(await this.usersService.getById(id));
}
```

## Rules

- Dates → ISO strings in DTOs (`toISOString()`).
- `_id` → `id` as hex string.
- Nested entities — map sub-documents or use `IdNameDto` helpers from `BaseMapper`.
- No mapping logic in controllers or services — keep in `mappers/`.

